{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AjhzGuDj43bhNM7rYFmeRY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tSPHINCS+\n2\t==========\n3\tThis repository contains a modified version of the [SPHINCS+ scheme reference](https://github.com/eyalr0/sphincsplusc/) including Jean-Philippe Aumasson's reference implementation of BLAKE.\n4\t\n5\tSPHINCS+ is a plausibly quantum resilient hash-based signature scheme which was selected by NIST for the [FIPS 205](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final) SLH-DSA \"Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard\" for post-quantum signatures.\n6\tThe SPHINCS+ construction combines multiple layers: Winternitz one-time signatures (WOTS+), a few-time signature scheme (FORS), Merkle trees, and a hypertree structure to enable scalable signing without state management.\n7\t\n8\t## Build Instructions\n9\tPrerequisites: \n10\t- libcrypto\n11\t\n12\t### Parameters\n13\tCMake requires three arguments to build the libraries.\n14\t- `HASH_BACKEND` Defining which underlying hash function to use `(blake, sha2, shake, haraka)` \n15\t- `THASH` Determining whether to use the robust or simple construction `(robust, simple)`\n16\t- `SECPAR` Determining the security parameter and whether to use short or fast signatures `(128f, 128s, 192f, 192s, 256f, 256s)`\n17\t\n18\tThe possible values are all listed in `CMakeLists.txt` with the exception of \n19\t`SECPAR`, which are formatted as the integer parameter with an appended character `s` or `f` indicating whether the signatures should prioritize length (short) or speed (fast). The integer parameter can either be 128, 192 or 256. An example `SECPAR` value is `128s`.\n20\t\n21\t### Build Commands\n22\tTo build for a particular set of parameters in a subdirectory `build`:\n23\t```\n24\tmdkir build\n25\tcmake -B build -DHASH_BACKEND=sha2 -DTHASH=robust -DSECPAR=192f\n26\tcmake --build build\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t## Associated Executable\n30\tFor testing purposes, there is a provided executable whose main function can be found in [PQCgenKAT_sign.c](./app/src/PQCgenKAT_sign.c). \n31\tThis executable performs an in-memory test of signing and verification capabilities before producing a shake256 digest of the signature transcripts.\n32\t\n33\tPQCgenKAT_sign.c links against the underlying hash backend with parameters defined by the CMake arguments `HASH_BACKEND`, `THASH`, and `SECPAR` described earlier.\n34\t\n35\t## License\n36\tFollowing the original code from the [SPHINCS+ submission repository](https://github.com/sphincs/sphincsplus), the [SPHINCS+ reference implementation](https://github.com/eyalr0/sphincsplusc/), and Jean-Philippe's BLAKE implementation, all included code is available under the CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication, with the exception of rng.c and rng.h which were provided by NIST, and PQCgenKAT_sign.c which was originally provided by NIST, but we have altered to no longer perform file IO.\n37\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3358c92a-c7cf-4ef9-adf3-e417cf8f446f","uuid":"649b6570-3f18-4d01-a04c-c4df9529fef8","timestamp":"2026-06-04T19:25:47.354Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-translate-lCHh9T/translated_rust/c_src/README.md","content":"SPHINCS+\n==========\nThis repository contains a modified version of the [SPHINCS+ scheme reference](https://github.com/eyalr0/sphincsplusc/) including Jean-Philippe Aumasson's reference implementation of BLAKE.\n\nSPHINCS+ is a plausibly quantum resilient hash-based signature scheme which was selected by NIST for the [FIPS 205](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final) SLH-DSA \"Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard\" for post-quantum signatures.\nThe SPHINCS+ construction combines multiple layers: Winternitz one-time signatures (WOTS+), a few-time signature scheme (FORS), Merkle trees, and a hypertree structure to enable scalable signing without state management.\n\n## Build Instructions\nPrerequisites: \n- libcrypto\n\n### Parameters\nCMake requires three arguments to build the libraries.\n- `HASH_BACKEND` Defining which underlying hash function to use `(blake, sha2, shake, haraka)` \n- `THASH` Determining whether to use the robust or simple construction `(robust, simple)`\n- `SECPAR` Determining the security parameter and whether to use short or fast signatures `(128f, 128s, 192f, 192s, 256f, 256s)`\n\nThe possible values are all listed in `CMakeLists.txt` with the exception of \n`SECPAR`, which are formatted as the integer parameter with an appended character `s` or `f` indicating whether the signatures should prioritize length (short) or speed (fast). The integer parameter can either be 128, 192 or 256. An example `SECPAR` value is `128s`.\n\n### Build Commands\nTo build for a particular set of parameters in a subdirectory `build`:\n```\nmdkir build\ncmake -B build -DHASH_BACKEND=sha2 -DTHASH=robust -DSECPAR=192f\ncmake --build build\n```\n\n## Associated Executable\nFor testing purposes, there is a provided executable whose main function can be found in [PQCgenKAT_sign.c](./app/src/PQCgenKAT_sign.c). \nThis executable performs an in-memory test of signing and verification capabilities before producing a shake256 digest of the signature transcripts.\n\nPQCgenKAT_sign.c links against the underlying hash backend with parameters defined by the CMake arguments `HASH_BACKEND`, `THASH`, and `SECPAR` described earlier.\n\n## License\nFollowing the original code from the [SPHINCS+ submission repository](https://github.com/sphincs/sphincsplus), the [SPHINCS+ reference implementation](https://github.com/eyalr0/sphincsplusc/), and Jean-Philippe's BLAKE implementation, all included code is available under the CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication, with the exception of rng.c and rng.h which were provided by NIST, and PQCgenKAT_sign.c which was originally provided by NIST, but we have altered to no longer perform file IO.\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
